<title>JAPAN: General Motors' unit launches 6.0% dual samurai.</title>
<headline>General Motors' unit launches 6.0% dual samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/New Zealand dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Merrill Lynch on Monday.</p>
<p>BORROWER General Motors Acceptance Corp (GMAC)</p>
<p>    AMT	30 bln yen</p>
<p>    COUPON   6.0 pct</p>
<p>    MATURITY 24 Dec 1998</p>
<p>TYPE dual samurai</p>
<p>ISS PRICEpar</p>
<p>PAY DATE24 Dec 1996</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Dec 2 to Dec 20</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P A-, Moody's A3</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGERS   Merrill Lynch, Kokusai Sec</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>Note: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive NZ$6,265.66</p>
<p>for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
